## 10. Reference Types

`java.lang.ref` lets you interact with reachability:

| Type | Cleared when | Typical use |
|---|---|---|
| Strong (normal) | Never while reachable | Everything |
| `SoftReference` | Under memory pressure | Memory-sensitive caches |
| `WeakReference` | At the next GC once only weakly reachable | Canonicalizing maps, listeners |
| `PhantomReference` | After the object is finalized, never returns the referent | Post-mortem cleanup |

```java
import java.lang.ref.*;

public class RefDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
        Object strong = new Object();
        WeakReference<Object> weak = new WeakReference<>(strong);

        System.out.println("Before: " + weak.get());  // non-null
        strong = null;
        System.gc();                                  // a hint, not a guarantee
        Thread.sleep(100);
        System.out.println("After:  " + weak.get());  // usually null
    }
}
```

`WeakHashMap` uses weak keys so entries vanish once the key is unreachable elsewhere:

```java
Map<Object, String> metadata = new WeakHashMap<>();
Object key = new Object();
metadata.put(key, "info");
key = null;
// After a GC, the entry can be removed automatically.
```

### Finalization Is Deprecated: Use `Cleaner`

`finalize()` is deprecated for removal (JEP 421, JDK 18). It is unpredictable, can resurrect objects, and delays reclamation by at least one GC cycle. Use `try-with-resources` for deterministic cleanup and `java.lang.ref.Cleaner` as a safety net:

```java
import java.lang.ref.Cleaner;

public class NativeBuffer implements AutoCloseable {
    private static final Cleaner CLEANER = Cleaner.create();

    // State must NOT reference the outer object, or it will never become phantom-reachable
    private static final class State implements Runnable {
        private long address;
        State(long address) { this.address = address; }
        @Override public void run() {
            if (address != 0) {
                freeNative(address);
                address = 0;
            }
        }
    }

    private final State state;
    private final Cleaner.Cleanable cleanable;

    public NativeBuffer(long size) {
        this.state = new State(allocateNative(size));
        this.cleanable = CLEANER.register(this, state);
    }

    @Override
    public void close() {
        cleanable.clean();   // deterministic; runs at most once
    }

    private static long allocateNative(long size) { /* ... */ return 1L; }
    private static void freeNative(long addr) { /* ... */ }
}
```

